<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Interactive Reading Guide for OpenStax Lifespan Development Chapter 11: Early Adulthood, Physical and Cognitive Development."><title>Module 10 | Early Adulthood — Interactive Reading Guide</title><style>
:root{--ink:#1a2c3d;--muted:#526779;--line:#d7e3e9;--navy:#173b55;--teal:#087b81;--pale:#edf7f7;--paper:#fff;--good:#176b4c;--warn:#8a5109}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f3f6f7;color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.58 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif}a{color:#075d77}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,textarea:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ec9f34;outline-offset:3px}header{background:linear-gradient(125deg,#12364f,#12696e);color:white;padding:2.4rem max(1rem,calc((100% - 1050px)/2)) 2rem}header .eyebrow{letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:800;opacity:.85}h1{font-size:clamp(1.7rem,4vw,2.7rem);line-height:1.15;margin:.65rem 0}header p{max-width:800px;margin:0;color:#e7f3f4}.wrap{max-width:1050px;padding:0 1rem 4rem;margin:auto}.toolstrip{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;background:white;padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;margin-top:-1.2rem;position:relative;box-shadow:0 4px 18px #163d5213}.toolstrip strong{display:block}.toolstrip small{color:var(--muted)}progress{width:min(350px,75vw);height:16px;accent-color:var(--teal)}button{cursor:pointer;border:0;border-radius:9px;padding:.64rem 1rem;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;font:inherit;font-weight:700}button:hover{background:#0b6373}button.secondary{background:#e7eff2;color:var(--navy)}button.secondary:hover{background:#d2e4e9}.quicknav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin:1.4rem 0}.quicknav a{text-decoration:none;border:1px solid #c7dbe2;background:white;padding:.45rem .7rem;border-radius:30px;font-size:.87rem;font-weight:700}.intro,.chapter{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem);margin:1.2rem 0}.intro{background:#eaf4f4}.chapter{scroll-margin-top:1rem}.sectiontop{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.kicker{color:var(--teal);font-weight:800;font-size:.83rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em}.chapter h2{font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1.25;margin:.25rem 0}.subtitle{color:var(--muted);margin:.1rem 0 .65rem;font-weight:600}.readlinks{margin:.85rem 0 1rem;display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.91rem}.item{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:1.4rem 0}.item h3{font-size:1.14rem;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 .85rem}.count{display:inline-block;color:var(--teal);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:.35rem}.choices{display:grid;gap:.56rem;margin:0 0 .8rem}.choice{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:.65rem;padding:.75rem .9rem;border:1px solid #ccd9df;border-radius:10px;cursor:pointer;background:#fafdfd}.choice:hover{border-color:var(--teal);background:#f3fafa}.choice:has(input:checked){border-color:#087b81;background:#e8f7f6}.choice input{margin-top:.33rem;accent-color:#087b81;transform:scale(1.13)}.feedback{border-left:4px solid var(--teal);margin-top:.8rem;padding:.7rem 1rem;background:#eaf4f4;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0}.feedback.wrong{border-color:#b47719;background:#fff5e6}.feedback[hidden]{display:none}.feedback b{display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem}.hint{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem}.answer{display:block;width:100%;min-height:110px;border:1px solid #aebfc8;border-radius:9px;padding:.8rem;font:inherit;resize:vertical;margin:.7rem 0}.details{margin-top:.8rem;border:1px solid #cbdfe2;border-radius:9px;padding:.65rem 1rem}.details summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy)}.complete{font-weight:800;color:var(--good);font-size:.9rem}.footer{text-align:center;color:var(--muted);padding:1rem}.finish{padding:1.4rem;border-radius:12px;background:#eaf4f4}.sr-only{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){html{scroll-behavior:smooth}}@media print{header{background:white;color:black;padding:0}.toolstrip,.quicknav,button{display:none!important}.chapter{break-inside:avoid}body{background:white}.feedback[hidden]{display:none}}
</style></head><body><header><div class="eyebrow">HD · Human Development &nbsp; | &nbsp; Interactive Reading Guide</div><h1>Module 10 · Early Adulthood:<br>Physical and Cognitive Development</h1><p>OpenStax Chapter 11 · Read, identify, apply, reconsider, and explain. Explore how biology, identity, thinking, relationships, and opportunity interact in adulthood.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="toolstrip"><div><strong id="progressText" aria-live="polite">0 of 16 activities completed</strong><small>Ungraded · Responses stay in this browser tab · About 20–25 minutes</small></div><div><progress id="progress" max="16" value="0" aria-label="Guide completion"></progress><div style="text-align:right;font-size:.85rem" id="percent">0%</div></div><button id="reset" class="secondary" type="button">Start over</button></div><nav class="quicknav" aria-label="Guide sections"><a href="#adult">11.1 Becoming an Adult</a><a href="#health">11.2–11.3 Health & Sexuality</a><a href="#thinking">11.4 Cognition</a><a href="#education">11.5 Education & Work</a><a href="#integrate">Synthesis</a></nav><div class="intro"><strong>How to use this guide</strong><p>Read each linked chapter section, then try its questions. Select an answer and choose <b>Check my thinking</b> to see a concept-based explanation. You can change an answer and check again. Written reflections are private self-checks: compare your thinking with a sample, not an automatic grade.</p><p><strong>Respectful learning:</strong> The chapter discusses sexual health, harassment, and personal identity. You are never required to disclose your own experiences. You may analyze the fictional cases instead. This guide does not send answers to Canvas or an instructor.</p><p><a href="https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-summary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStax Chapter 11 summary ↗</a></p></div><div id="sections"></div><div class="finish" id="finish" aria-live="polite"><strong>Keep going</strong><p>Complete the activities across all five sections to finish the guide. You can revisit and revise anything.</p></div><div class="footer">Adapted for CLDV-01 from OpenStax <i>Lifespan Development</i>, Chapter 11. Original practice questions and fictional cases. This is an independent, ungraded learning guide.</div></main><script>
const sections = [{"id": "adult", "number": "11.1", "title": "Becoming an Adult", "subtitle": "Identity, commitments, and different pathways", "intro": "Emerging adulthood is often described as a period of exploration, but opportunities to explore depend on social, cultural, and economic circumstances.", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-1-becoming-an-adult", "qs": [{"kind": "single", "q": "Jalen, 22, says: “I am trying different career paths and learning what matters to me, but I haven’t committed to one.” Which identity status fits best?", "options": ["Identity achievement", "Identity foreclosure", "Identity moratorium", "Identity diffusion"], "answer": 2, "why": "Moratorium combines active exploration with no settled commitment. Achievement includes commitment after exploration; foreclosure involves commitment without exploration."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "Which situation best illustrates Arnett’s “feeling in-between” characteristic?", "options": ["A 20-year-old feels responsible for personal choices but not yet fully established as an adult.", "A 20-year-old has no relationships with people of other ages.", "A 20-year-old has finished all possible identity exploration.", "A 20-year-old must be financially independent to qualify as an adult."], "answer": 0, "why": "Feeling in-between refers to a subjective sense of being partly adult while still building adult roles; it does not require any one living arrangement."}, {"kind": "multi", "q": "Which factors can shape whether a person has time and resources to explore adult pathways? Select all that apply.", "options": ["Family caregiving responsibilities", "Tuition costs and paid-work obligations", "Cultural expectations about adulthood", "The idea that everyone must leave home by age 18"], "answer": [0, 1, 2], "why": "Caregiving, economic access, and culture shape opportunities. No universal deadline requires a person to leave home at 18."}]}, {"id": "health", "number": "11.2–11.3", "title": "Physical Health and Sexuality", "subtitle": "Body changes, healthy habits, respectful relationships", "intro": "Physical capacities often reach high levels in early adulthood, but habits and circumstances influence lifelong health. Sexuality includes identity, attraction, behavior, and relationship choices.", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-2-physical-health-and-growth-in-early-adulthood", "extra": "https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-3-sexuality-in-early-adulthood", "qs": [{"kind": "single", "q": "Which statement best reflects typical physical development in early adulthood?", "options": ["All body systems begin a rapid decline at age 18.", "Many physical capacities are strong, while maturation and gradual changes continue.", "Physical development stops completely once puberty ends.", "Exercise cannot affect physical well-being after adolescence."], "answer": 1, "why": "Several systems mature or function near their peak in these years, but development and individual variation continue."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "Elisa works evening shifts and sleeps irregularly. She feels exhausted in class. Which response best connects this situation to the chapter?", "options": ["Young adults need less sleep, so fatigue is unrelated to routine.", "Academic success matters more than any health behavior.", "Only genetic factors can shape long-term adult health.", "Sleep, stress, and daily routines can affect health now and later."], "answer": 3, "why": "Sleep and stress are important health influences in early adulthood. A realistic plan should consider work demands and available supports."}, {"kind": "multi", "q": "Which statements accurately distinguish dimensions of sexuality? Select all that apply.", "options": ["Gender identity and sexual orientation are different concepts.", "Knowing someone’s gender identity tells you their sexual orientation.", "Sexuality can involve identity, attraction, feelings, and behavior.", "Respectful communication and consent matter in relationships."], "answer": [0, 2, 3], "why": "Identity and orientation are distinct. Sexuality is broader than sexual activity, and voluntary consent and communication are essential in relationships."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "Two adults are discussing sexual health. Which choice is most consistent with informed, respectful decision-making?", "options": ["Assume risk is impossible when a relationship feels serious.", "Avoid discussion because sexual health is always private.", "Discuss boundaries, consent, and appropriate prevention or testing.", "Treat one person’s choices as universally correct for everyone."], "answer": 2, "why": "Open, voluntary communication and informed prevention help people navigate sexual health. There is no single prescribed relationship path."}]}, {"id": "thinking", "number": "11.4", "title": "Thinking in Early Adulthood", "subtitle": "Evidence, experience, multiple perspectives", "intro": "Maya, a community college student, hopes to transfer to a university. She also works many hours and helps her family with transportation. A counselor helps her weigh options rather than deciding for her.", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-4-cognitive-development-in-early-adulthood", "qs": [{"kind": "single", "q": "What is the counselor’s strongest next step with Maya?", "options": ["Tell Maya that family obligations must always take priority.", "Compare goals, constraints, evidence, and several workable pathways.", "Insist that the university option is best for every student.", "Delay the conversation until all uncertainty disappears."], "answer": 1, "why": "Postformal thought takes competing values, real-world constraints, and ambiguity seriously rather than assuming one abstract rule fits everyone."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "One person argues that full-time work provides stability. Another says college offers future opportunity. Maya considers part-time enrollment combined with work. This is an example of…", "options": ["Dialectical thinking", "Identity foreclosure", "Speed of processing", "Automatic reflexes"], "answer": 0, "why": "Dialectical thinking can integrate apparently competing views into a more nuanced position."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "Maya hears that “all transfer credits are guaranteed” but checks official articulation agreements and asks an advisor before deciding. Which process is most evident?", "options": ["Diffusion of identity", "An unexamined heuristic", "Reflective thought", "A fixed developmental timetable"], "answer": 2, "why": "Reflective thought evaluates claims against evidence and revises conclusions when warranted."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "Maya’s employer offers a reliable two-day schedule; a relative can now help with transportation. Transfer costs remain uncertain. What should Maya do?", "options": ["Transfer immediately because all barriers are gone.", "Ignore the new supports to avoid changing a plan.", "Allow someone else to decide because support was offered.", "Reassess the options with the new supports and unresolved costs."], "answer": 3, "why": "Flexible reasoning updates a decision when relevant facts change without pretending that every uncertainty has disappeared."}]}, {"id": "education", "number": "11.5", "title": "Higher Education and Work", "subtitle": "Opportunity, access, and meaningful choices", "intro": "Educational and career pathways are shaped by resources, opportunity, interests, commitments, and institutional conditions. There is no single route that works for everyone.", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-5-contexts-higher-education-and-work-achievement-in-early-adulthood", "qs": [{"kind": "single", "q": "Which statement most accurately reflects the chapter’s view of postsecondary pathways?", "options": ["A four-year university is the only path to adult success.", "Career choice depends only on individual motivation.", "College, apprenticeships, and technical programs can each be viable paths.", "Education is unrelated to economic and cultural opportunities."], "answer": 2, "why": "Education can support opportunity, but cost, access, work, and personal goals influence which pathway is feasible and meaningful."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "A peer tells Maya, “Just follow your passion.” What is missing from that advice?", "options": ["Consideration of finances, time, relationships, and available supports.", "The assumption that the counselor should pick Maya’s career.", "A guarantee that every graduate receives the same salary.", "A rule that ambition should outweigh family circumstances."], "answer": 0, "why": "Interests matter, but plans also require attention to material constraints and possible supports."}, {"kind": "single", "q": "Two students make different training decisions: one chooses a paid apprenticeship and the other a transfer degree. What is the best developmental interpretation?", "options": ["The apprenticeship student has failed to explore identity.", "Different resources and goals can make different paths reasonable.", "The transfer student is necessarily more cognitively mature.", "Both decisions must lead to the same career outcome."], "answer": 1, "why": "Adult pathways reflect personal goals as well as contextual resources; a single educational choice does not prove maturity."}]}, {"id": "integrate", "number": "Synthesis", "title": "Connect the Chapter", "subtitle": "Apply multiple ideas to a new situation", "intro": "These final reflections are ungraded. Use specific developmental terms and reasoning rather than seeking one perfect answer.", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/lifespan-development/pages/11-summary", "qs": [{"kind": "reflection", "q": "New case: Alex, 24, is exploring a health-care career while working evenings, supporting a younger sibling, and trying to improve sleep. Explain how TWO different Chapter 11 concepts help you understand Alex’s situation.", "hint": "Consider identity exploration, emerging adulthood, health habits, or contextual influences.", "example": "Alex may be in identity moratorium because they are actively exploring a career without a settled commitment. Their irregular sleep illustrates how everyday responsibilities and health habits can interact during early adulthood."}, {"kind": "reflection", "q": "Return to Maya. Identify one new piece of evidence that could change her transfer decision. Explain why revising her plan could reflect mature cognition, not indecision.", "hint": "Use a concept such as reflective, dialectical, or postformal thinking.", "example": "A verified financial-aid award might change what Maya can afford. Reflective thought means evaluating credible evidence, while postformal reasoning recognizes that the strongest choice depends partly on circumstances."}]}];
const completed=new Set();
const root=document.querySelector('#sections');
let index=0;
function safe(t){return String(t).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));}
for(const s of sections){const part=document.createElement('section');part.className='chapter';part.id=s.id;let extra=s.extra?`<a href="${s.extra}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read §11.3 ↗</a>`:'';part.innerHTML=`<div class="sectiontop"><span class="kicker">Section ${s.number}</span><span class="complete" id="done-${s.id}">0 of ${s.qs.length} complete</span></div><h2>${safe(s.title)}</h2><p class="subtitle">${safe(s.subtitle)}</p><p>${safe(s.intro)}</p><div class="readlinks"><a href="${s.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read section ↗</a>${extra}</div>`;for(const q of s.qs){index++;const key='q'+index;const item=document.createElement('div');item.className='item';item.dataset.key=key;item.dataset.section=s.id;const answerType=q.kind==='multi'?'checkbox':'radio';let work='';if(q.kind==='reflection'){work=`<p class="hint">${safe(q.hint)}</p><label class="sr-only" for="${key}-text">Your reflection</label><textarea class="answer" id="${key}-text" placeholder="Write a few sentences here (optional)."></textarea><button type="button" data-check="${key}">Compare my thinking</button><details class="details" id="${key}-sample" hidden><summary>Sample response for comparison</summary><p>${safe(q.example)}</p></details>`;}else{work=`<div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Answer options">${q.options.map((v,j)=>`<label class="choice"><input type="${answerType}" name="${key}" value="${j}"><span>${safe(v)}</span></label>`).join('')}</div><button type="button" data-check="${key}">Check my thinking</button><div id="${key}-feedback" class="feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>`;}item.innerHTML=`<span class="count">Activity ${index} of 16</span><h3>${safe(q.q)}</h3>${work}`;item._question=q;part.appendChild(item);}root.appendChild(part);}
function update(){const n=completed.size;document.querySelector('#progressText').textContent=`${n} of 16 activities completed`;document.querySelector('#progress').value=n;document.querySelector('#percent').textContent=Math.round(n/16*100)+'%';for(const s of sections){const count=[...document.querySelectorAll(`[data-section="${s.id}"]`)].filter(el=>completed.has(el.dataset.key)).length;document.getElementById('done-'+s.id).textContent=`${count} of ${s.qs.length} complete`;}document.querySelector('#finish').innerHTML=n===16?'<strong>✓ Guide complete!</strong><p>You explored all five major chapter sections and applied developmental concepts to real-life decisions. Review any explanations you want to revisit before class.</p>':'<strong>Keep going</strong><p>Complete the activities across all five sections to finish the guide. You can revisit and revise anything.</p>';}
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{const btn=e.target.closest('[data-check]');if(!btn)return;const key=btn.dataset.check;const item=document.querySelector(`[data-key="${key}"]`);const q=item._question;if(q.kind==='reflection'){document.getElementById(key+'-sample').hidden=false;completed.add(key);btn.textContent='View sample below';update();return;}const picked=[...item.querySelectorAll('input:checked')].map(x=>Number(x.value));const f=document.getElementById(key+'-feedback');if(!picked.length){f.hidden=false;f.className='feedback wrong';f.innerHTML='<b>Select an answer first.</b>Then check your reasoning.';return;}const correct=q.kind==='single'?picked.length===1&&picked[0]===q.answer:picked.length===q.answer.length&&picked.every(x=>q.answer.includes(x));f.hidden=false;f.className='feedback'+(correct?'':' wrong');f.innerHTML=`<b>${correct?'✓ Well reasoned.':'Not quite — reconsider the distinctions.'}</b>${safe(q.why)}`;if(correct){completed.add(key);}else{completed.delete(key);}update();});
document.getElementById('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(!confirm('Clear all selections and reflections in this guide?'))return;document.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(x=>x.checked=false);document.querySelectorAll('textarea').forEach(x=>x.value='');document.querySelectorAll('.feedback').forEach(x=>x.hidden=true);document.querySelectorAll('.details').forEach(x=>x.hidden=true);document.querySelectorAll('[data-check]').forEach(x=>{if(x.closest('.item')._question.kind==='reflection')x.textContent='Compare my thinking';});completed.clear();update();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'});});update();
</script></body></html>
